# 3. User Roles and Permissions

The platform currently has three primary roles:

- Customer
- Contractor
- Admin

## 3.1 Admin

Admin has complete catalog management permissions.

Admin can:

- View all material categories.
- Create material categories.
- Edit material categories.
- Activate or deactivate material categories.
- View all materials.
- Create materials.
- Edit materials.
- Activate or deactivate materials.
- Archive eligible materials.
- View all service categories.
- Create service categories.
- Edit service categories.
- Activate or deactivate service categories.
- View all services.
- Create services.
- Edit services.
- Activate or deactivate services.
- Manage material compatibility.
- Manage service compatibility.
- Search and filter catalog information.

## 3.2 Customer

Customers have no catalog management permissions.

During Phase 5, customers should not receive catalog editing interfaces.

Future phases may use catalog information while creating estimates.

## 3.3 Contractor

Contractors have no catalog management permissions.

Contractors must not be able to:

- Create materials.
- Modify material costs.
- Modify coverage rates.
- Create services.
- Change service information.
- Modify material compatibility.
- Activate or deactivate catalog records.

Future phases may allow contractors to view selected catalog information when working with authorized projects.

## 3.4 Authorization Rules

All catalog write operations must require:

- Valid authentication.
- Admin role.
- Backend authorization.

Frontend route protection is not sufficient.

Every write operation must be independently protected by backend middleware.

Never trust a role or user ID supplied by the frontend.

