# 4. Material Category Management

## 4.1 Purpose

Material categories organize restoration products into logical groups.

Examples:

1. Wood Stains
2. Paints
3. Protective Coatings
4. Sealers
5. Primers
6. Cleaning Products
7. Surface Preparation Products
8. Repair Materials
9. Composite Deck Products
10. Other Materials

These are suggested initial categories, not a mandatory fixed list.

Admin must be able to manage categories dynamically.

## 4.2 Material Category Fields

Each material category should contain:

| Field | Description | Validation |
|---|---|---|
| name | Category name | Required, unique |
| slug | URL-friendly identifier | Required, unique |
| description | Category description | Optional |
| displayOrder | Display position | Non-negative integer |
| status | Category status | active/inactive |
| createdAt | Creation timestamp | System-generated |
| updatedAt | Last update timestamp | System-generated |
| createdBy | Admin who created it | System-generated |
| updatedBy | Admin who updated it | System-generated |

## 4.3 Category Rules

- Category names must be unique after normalization.
- Slugs must be unique.
- Category names must be trimmed.
- Empty names must be rejected.
- Inactive categories must not be available for new material assignments.
- Existing materials must not be silently deleted when a category becomes inactive.
- A category with associated materials should not be permanently deleted.
- Prefer deactivation or archival.

