# 16. Validation Rules

Backend validation is mandatory.

Frontend validation improves usability but must never replace backend validation.

## 16.1 General Validation

- Required strings must not be empty.
- Strings must be trimmed.
- Unknown request properties must be rejected.
- MongoDB IDs must be validated.
- Enum values must be restricted.
- Numeric fields must be finite.
- Negative values must be rejected where inappropriate.
- Text fields must have maximum lengths.
- Duplicate names and codes must be handled safely.

## 16.2 Material Validation

- Material name is required.
- Material code is required and unique.
- Category must exist.
- Category must be active for new material creation.
- Material type must be valid.
- Compatible surfaces must use supported values.
- Coverage values must be positive when supplied.
- Coverage units must be valid.
- Cost must be non-negative when supplied.
- Currency must be a supported configured value.
- Status must be valid.

## 16.3 Service Validation

- Service name is required.
- Service code is required and unique.
- Category must exist.
- Category must be active for new service creation.
- Service type must be valid.
- Measurement unit must be valid.
- Estimated duration must be positive when supplied.
- Status must be valid.

## 16.4 Compatibility Validation

- Material ID is required.
- Service ID is required.
- Both referenced records must exist.
- Duplicate pairs must be rejected.
- Compatibility status must be valid.
- Compatibility notes must have a maximum length.

## 16.5 Update Validation

PATCH requests must support partial updates.

However:

- Immutable fields must not be changed by unauthorized payloads.
- Unknown properties must be rejected.
- Category references must be revalidated.
- Status transitions must be validated.
- A partial update must not unintentionally erase unrelated fields.

